&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chime is on a mission to help millions of everyday people achieve financial progress — and we&#39;ve built one of the strongest digital acquisition organizations in the industry to get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of Growth and Acquisition owns what comes next: leading the full digital acquisition portfolio — paid social, paid search, affiliate, YouTube, mobile and app networks, and emerging channels — while building the capabilities that define Chime&#39;s next chapter of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role, not a channel-management role. The foundation — building great teams, running healthy channels, and consistently delivering results — doesn&#39;t change. What changes is the mandate: this leader is accountable for delivering today&#39;s business while identifying and building tomorrow&#39;s growth engine, staying close enough to the ecosystem of platforms, agencies, and technology partners to bring new capabilities into Chime before they become table stakes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within Chime&#39;s newly evolved Media &amp;amp; Acquisition organization, alongside a Director of Media leading Offline, Media Planning, and MMM. Together, these two roles are being broadened in scope as Chime moves from a channel-by-channel model toward a more complete, portfolio-level view of how every marketing dollar creates value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary offered for this role and level of experience will begin at $196,000.00 and up to $270,000.00. Full-time employees are also eligible for a bonus, competitive equity package, and benefits. The actual base salary offered may be higher, depending on your location, skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;In this role, you can expect to&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own performance across Chime&#39;s full digital acquisition portfolio (paid social, paid search, affiliate, YouTube, mobile/app networks, and emerging channels), delivering ambitious growth, efficiency, and CAC targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make portfolio-level investment and prioritization calls across channels, talent, technology, and vendor partnerships, balancing near-term performance against long-term capability building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of experienced channel managers as a true player-coach — close enough to the work to challenge assumptions and unblock hard problems, but focused on multiplying impact through people and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build new acquisition channels, partnerships, or technology-enabled growth motions — not just optimize the existing mix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay plugged into the external digital ecosystem — platforms, agencies, AI/martech vendors, startups — to identify opportunities before they&#39;re obvious and bring new capability into Chime early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push the organization to rebuild how it works around AI: experimentation, creative production, media buying, and measurement — not just point-solution automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Media Planning/MMM, Growth Product Marketing, Analytics, Risk, and Finance to align channel strategy to company-level growth and CAC goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Digital Acquisition in senior leadership forums, translating channel performance into business outcomes for Growth LT, EC, and Board-level audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;To thrive in this role, you have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a multi-channel digital acquisition or growth organization with meaningful business accountability — not only channel-level metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated record of owning growth, efficiency, and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a significant media portfolio and making prioritization tradeoffs across channels, technology, and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A leadership style that blends strategic range with hands-on credibility — comfortable operating as both strategist and player-coach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling teams and developing future leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-moving, cross-functional, senior-executive-visible environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-AM1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A little about us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
