&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Lifecycle Marketing Manager to join our Product and Lifecycle Marketing team. In this role, you&#39;ll design and optimize lifecycle programs that engage, retain, and grow members across their entire journey with Chime—from top of funnel through long-term retention—with a clear focus on driving growth, revenue, and member lifetime value (LTV).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a holistic, business-minded marketer rather than a single-channel specialist. You&#39;ll think in terms of segments, experiments, and outcomes: building targeted campaigns across the channels we own—push, in-app, and out-of-app (email, SMS)—while connecting those touchpoints with the broader, non-owned channels that shape the member experience. You&#39;ll partner closely with cross-functional teams to turn data into segmentation, automation, and personalization strategies that move the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role with department-level impact: you&#39;ll own diverse projects, exercise significant independent judgment, and influence how members experience Chime across the full lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re creative, dedicated, and love working in a fast-paced environment alongside passionate colleagues, we want to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary offered for this role and level of experience will begin at $139,000 and up to $181,000. Full-time employees are also eligible for a bonus, competitive equity package, and benefits. The actual base salary offered may be higher, depending on your location, skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you can expect to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full-funnel lifecycle strategy—from top of funnel through activation and long-term retention—building targeted campaigns that drive growth, revenue, and member LTV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define segments and translate them into targeted, personalized campaigns across owned channels (push, in-app, and out-of-app), connecting them with the broader non-owned channels that shape the end-to-end member experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate data-driven hypotheses and run experiments to continuously optimize evergreen lifecycle campaigns and transactional communications, working with analytics to measure impact, socialize findings, and develop next steps toward bigger wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and steward channel guidelines and governance, preserving the quality and integrity of our communications ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and build strong relationships with partners across Product, Product Marketing, Engineering, Analytics, Design, User Research, CRM, and more to develop and deliver on shared strategies for large cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To thrive in this role, you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6+ years of experience in lifecycle, growth, or related marketing, developing end-to-end campaigns from conceptualization to measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growth-oriented, business-first mindset—you think about revenue, LTV, and the full funnel, not just individual channels, and you can connect owned channels (push, in-app, out-of-app) with the broader member experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of building segments and managing successful campaigns across multiple channels (email, push, SMS, in-app messaging).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experimentation chops—comfortable with A/B testing and using results to inform what to scale next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with experience in data-driven marketing and performance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work cross-functionally and collaborate with various stakeholders, exercising significant independent judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with key marketing platforms (Braze, Looker; AI tools a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong self-starter mindset—adaptable and able to think critically to develop creative solutions with limited resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
