&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a mobile platform engineer, you&#39;ll help shape the future of Chime&#39;s React Native app, building the infrastructure and tooling that make development faster, safer, and more scalable for hundreds of engineers working alongside AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in this role if you enjoy building for developers, solving complex technical problems, and multiplying your impact on others while delivering a best-of-class experience for our 10M+ monthly active members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary offered for this role and level of experience will begin at $164,000.00 and up to $227,000.00. Full-time employees are also eligible for a bonus, competitive equity package, and benefits. The actual base salary offered may be higher, depending on your location, skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you can expect to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain internal frameworks, developer tooling, and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product and engineering teams to improve app quality, performance, and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify bottlenecks and deploy operational efficiencies to automate mobile CI/CD and release orchestration, reducing manual effort and increasing reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and improve tooling to reduce friction in the developer loop and maximize engineering velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and raise the bar on technical standards, code quality, and delivery practices through design reviews, guidance, and example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with QA to lead Chime’s mobile release process across iOS and Android.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale AI-enabling app development&amp;nbsp; infrastructure to support increased product velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To thrive in this role, you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in cross-platform, mobile development,&amp;nbsp; ideally with React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset, excellent communication skills, and a drive to document and share what you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fluency in TypeScript and familiarity with React, React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with iOS and Android build, configuration, and distribution systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped apps that are used by millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of profiling and improving app performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with observability and analytics tools like Bugsnag, Datadog, Sentry, or Hex.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of server-client architecture, leveraging GraphQL and performance profiling (e.g., memory pressure, screen latency, optimizing time to interactive, preloading).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile build infrastructure platforms such as Bitrise, CircleCI, or GitHub Actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with feature flag systems, runtime controls, or OTA delivery frameworks (e.g., Expo Updates, CodePush).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building the infrastructure that supports AI-native mobile development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with state management tools like Redux, React Context, AsyncStorage, or MMKV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaled mobile quality practices and testing frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
