&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; on the &lt;strong&gt;AI Enablement&lt;/strong&gt; team, you will contribute to the internal platforms, primitives, and guardrails that make AI a trusted co-pilot for employees across Chime.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll work on systems like &lt;strong&gt;Archimedes, Bosun&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;easyRAG&lt;/strong&gt; that power internal AI assistants, developer workflows, and retrieval-backed applications. These platforms make it easier for teams across the company to build, adopt, and scale LLM-powered tools safely and effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team defines Chime&#39;s golden paths for AI: opinionated but flexible patterns that help teams move quickly while maintaining safety, reliability, cost control, and governance. In this role, you&#39;ll build on and extend these patterns — shipping real features on production AI platforms while developing your depth in AI-specific engineering practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll collaborate with &lt;strong&gt;Platform Engineering, Security, Risk, Legal&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;product &lt;/strong&gt;teams to build scalable, well-governed systems that support internal AI use cases from early prototyping through production adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary offered for this role and level of experience will begin at &lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt;$133,000.00&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp; and up to &lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt;$184,000.00.&lt;/span&gt; Full-time employees are also eligible for a bonus, competitive equity package, and benefits. The actual base salary offered may be higher, depending on your location, skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;In this role, you can expect to&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and extend internal AI platforms such as Archimedes, Bosun, and easyRAG, helping teams develop and scale LLM-powered applications and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable platform capabilities such as APIs, SDKs, templates, and shared services that make it easier to develop safe, high-quality AI-powered tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype and productionize new AI capabilities alongside senior engineers, turning successful patterns into durable platform features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Chime&#39;s golden path patterns for LLM usage, and help refine them as you deepen familiarity with the systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build features that let teams launch AI-powered assistants and workflows in a standardized, observable, and governed way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and apply evaluation, observability, and cost-management practices across AI systems — including quality, latency, safety, and spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security, Risk, and Legal to implement guardrails for responsible AI development and usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineers across Chime to embed AI into internal tools, workflows, and employee experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;To thrive in this role, you have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a software engineer with a track record of shipping production-quality features in a distributed system or platform environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working with LLMs or ML services, or strong curiosity and a demonstrated ability to ramp quickly into AI-specific tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid coding skills in at least one of Python, Go, or TypeScript/JavaScript, with comfort working across services, CLIs, and internal tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An emerging platform mindset: you think about reuse and building for more than one consumer, not just solving the immediate problem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with — or eagerness to learn — AI-specific engineering concerns such as evaluation, prompt and version management, observability, cost control, safety, and data privacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain technical tradeoffs to teammates and cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
